        "original_id": "05dff770-9b97-52d4-aa0e-c1409b77b347",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Ludwig van Beethoven, Heinrich August Marschner\n- Works: Turkish March, \"The Elephant Never Forgets\"\n- Products: Moog Indigo\n- Programs: El Chavo del Ocho\n- Topics: German classical music, German opera, cover versions, theme songs\n\nFacts:\n- Ludwig van Beethoven was baptised on 17 December 1770 and died on 26 March 1827.\n- Ludwig van Beethoven was a German composer and pianist.\n- Heinrich August Marschner was born on 16 August 1795 and died on 14 December 1861.\n- Heinrich August Marschner was the most important composer of German opera between Weber and Wagner.\n- The Turkish March, also called Marcia alla turca, is a well-known classical march theme by Ludwig van Beethoven.\n- The ninth selection on Moog Indigo is a cover of Beethoven's Turkish March titled \"The Elephant Never Forgets.\"\n- \"The Elephant Never Forgets\" was used as the theme song for El Chavo del Ocho.",
